the cross tourer is billed as an all  roads version of a Citroen c5 wagon  it comes with an array of driver assists  fitted a standard and a classic set to  an gimmick first impressions our car  reviewer Montes finds it a bit odd the  way the steering wheel turns but the  center section does not and again if you  have a collision while going around a  bend you can be sure the airbag will  deploy straight at you  meaning proper protection so it is  practical is one pocket  the c5 has a reputation for sound  handling the cross term makes no secret  of its weight however the handling is  such reflects how big and heavy the  color is montes finds it a bit sluggish  the steering response is a little  indirect although you don't feel as if  it's unsafe the Crosstour comes with a  choice of three diesel engines the HDI  165 we tested is the second most  powerful option generating 120 kilowatts  and propelling the car to 100 km/h in  9.3 seconds official fuel consumption is  5.1 liters overall Mathis likes the  interior workmanship some sections are a  bit sloppy like this edge of plastic  sticking out light colored thing poking  out by the fan except for those minor  cosmetic flaws the interior works  the cars exterior look is enlivened by  fender flares long roof bars and 18-inch  alloy wheels chrome effect wing mirror  caps and brushed metal style protective  trim on the front and rear skirting add  a touch of French chick to the new sit  when the cargo section encompasses 533  litres a nice feature is the detachable  trunk lamp doubling up as a practical  flashlight  the interior is uncluttered with a  pleasant touch to the materials the  driver is particularly pampered with the  heated seat also boasting a massage  function the high directive three-plus  suspension can be raised by six or four  centimetres to boost the car's off-road  caliber albeit only at speeds under 40  km/h Montes isn't really satisfied on  the one hand you can raise the body  really high which is very practical on  rough terrain but with a slightest bit  of rain you can't go off-road  front-wheel power means insufficient  traction the Crosstour has its strengths  the dynamic exterior the hydropneumatic  suspension and the smart assists but it  also has its drawbacks a 37 thousand  euro price tag in Germany means the  Citroen c5 cross tourer is no bargain  but not that expensive either if a word  for the restriction to front-wheel drive  the idea would be perfect perfect
 

